From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:59:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] screenshot: no screencast service where the session mode
 cannot screencast

Upstream bug fix, not an Apex change: drop this patch once upstream's
ScreenshotUI stops activating org.gnome.Shell.Screencast in session
modes without allowScreencast.

ScreenshotUI creates its ScreencastProxy at startup in every session
mode, so D-Bus starts the screencast service in the greeter and in
initial setup too, though neither mode can screencast: the cast button
needs allowScreencast. The service initialises GStreamer and GTK; with
the greeter's home on gdm's tmpfs, GStreamer rebuilds its plugin
registry on every greeter start. Where the mode cannot screencast, the
proxy no longer auto-starts the service.
---
 js/ui/screenshot.js | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/js/ui/screenshot.js b/js/ui/screenshot.js
index 02560b9..57b8889 100644
--- a/js/ui/screenshot.js
+++ b/js/ui/screenshot.js
@@ -1532,7 +1532,9 @@ export class ScreenshotUI extends St.Widget {
 
                 this._screencastSupported = this._screencastProxy.ScreencastSupported;
                 this._syncCastButton();
-            });
+            },
+            null,
+            Main.sessionMode.allowScreencast ? Gio.DBusProxyFlags.NONE : Gio.DBusProxyFlags.DO_NOT_AUTO_START);
 
         this._screencastProxy.connectSignal('Error', (proxy, sender, [errorName, message]) =>
             this._screencastFailed(ScreencastPhase.RECORDING,
